    "created_at": "2016-03-29T15:29:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-29T15:29:23Z",
    "body": "`<textarea>` is a replaced element. Any CSS that applies only does so by the grace of god.  But we specifically call out \"white-space\" because it's a property that can usefully apply to a textarea in any conceivable rational presentation of the widget, and is useful, and so it makes sense to require browsers to support it. overflow-wrap is in the same boat.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
